    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "That makes sense. When we look closer at District 2, we want to differentiate between the environmental risk and the actual behavior of the residents. Some of our preliminary notes suggest that the high density isn't the only factor—there are mentions of specific cultural lifestyles and traditional social structures in these immigrant communities that might impact transmission. \n\nIn your modeling, how much weight should we give to these cultural or lifestyle differences versus just the physical density/transit factors? Do you think certain community behaviors or hygiene practices typical of these specific groups could accelerate the spread more than the housing itself?",
